---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
import { componentsSidebar } from '../../data/nav';
import withHintHtml from '../../examples/select/with-hint.html?raw';
import withErrorHtml from '../../examples/select/with-error.html?raw';
import disabledHtml from '../../examples/select/disabled.html?raw';

const onThisPage = [
  { label: 'Preview', href: '#preview' },
  { label: 'When to use', href: '#when-to-use' },
  { label: 'When not to use', href: '#when-not-to-use' },
  { label: 'Guidance', href: '#guidance' },
  { label: 'Errors', href: '#errors' },
  { label: 'Disabled selects', href: '#disabled-selects' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Select"
  section="components"
  description="Use the select component to let users choose one option from a long list."
  pageTitle="Select"
  pageSubtitle="Lets users choose one option from a long, familiar list."
  sidebarGroups={componentsSidebar}
  sidebarLabel="Components"
  onThisPage={onThisPage}
>
  <div class="govbb-prose">
    <h2 id="preview">Preview</h2>
  </div>
  <Example title="Select with hint text" html={withHintHtml.trim()} />

  <div class="govbb-prose">
    <p>
      The Select component is a dropdown that lets users choose a single option from a
      long list, such as a parish or a country. It is a last resort for long lists —
      most questions are easier to answer with visible options.
    </p>

    <h2 id="when-to-use">When to use this component</h2>
    <p>
      Use a select when there are more than about five options and the list is one
      users already know, such as a parish or a month. Selects work well when the
      options are long and predictable enough that hiding them behind a dropdown does
      not slow users down.
    </p>

    <h2 id="when-not-to-use">When not to use this component</h2>
    <p>
      Do not use a select for five or fewer options — radio buttons show every choice
      at once and are easier to scan and select. Do not use a select for data users
      would want to search for, such as a long list of countries, without also
      offering a typeahead. And do not use a select when more than one answer is
      allowed — use checkboxes instead.
    </p>

    <h2 id="guidance">Guidance</h2>
    <p>
      Start the list with a non-selectable placeholder option, such as <em
        >"Select a parish"</em
      >, so users make an active choice rather than submitting a default value by
      accident.
    </p>
    <p>
      Always pair a select with a visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>. Use hint text (<code
        >.govbb-hint</code
      >) beneath the label to explain what is being asked, and link it to the select
      with <code>aria-describedby</code>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
    <p>
      When a select fails validation, show an error message (<code
        >.govbb-error-message</code
      >) above the select with <code>role="alert"</code>, and mark the select itself
      with <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> pointing
      at the error message id. Keep error messages specific and actionable, such as
      "Select a parish".
    </p>
  </div>
  <Example title="Select with error" html={withErrorHtml.trim()} />

  <div class="govbb-prose">
    <h2 id="disabled-selects">Disabled selects</h2>
    <p>
      Avoid disabling selects wherever possible. A disabled select gives the user no
      information about what they need to do to enable it, and its content is skipped
      by many screen readers. Prefer showing the value as read-only text, or explaining
      why the field is unavailable.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Example title="Disabled select" html={disabledHtml.trim()} />
</ArticleLayout>
